VIOLATION — rule-authoring.md. Four breaches, all in the clause body; everything outside it
is shared with the sibling pole and is not a finding.

1. MODAL MISMATCH — the heading states an obligation ("MUST Carry An Attestation") while the
   body hedges throughout: should generally, encouraged to move toward, usually less
   informative, tends to be worth avoiding, may reasonably treat. The closing sentence then
   hands back the exact case the heading forbids, permitting the TTL extension where the
   successor is the same operator or the lease has been uncontested — which is the whole
   content of the rule, returned as an exception.

2. ABSTRACT BLOCKED CORPUS — the `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading is present and
   holds six CATEGORY LABELS ("Convenience-based reasoning about record keeping",
   "Deferral arguments framed around reconstruction being possible later") instead of the
   literal first-person sentences an agent emits. A corpus of taxonomy labels traps nothing
   at the moment the excuse is being formed.

3. NON-CONTRASTING WORKED BLOCK — the DO and DO-NOT arms are the SAME record line. They
   differ only in the trailing adverbs, promptly and belatedly. The contrast slot is filled
   and carries no contrast, so nothing is learnable from the block.

4. OVER-LONG JUSTIFICATION — the `**Why:**` runs well past the two-sentence cap and wanders
   into archive rotation, multi-template programmes, reviewer rotation and staffing, none of
   which is the mechanism the clause turns on.

SHARED FURNITURE — NOT FINDINGS. The frontmatter, the entire MUST NOT section including its
justification, the whole Trust Posture Wiring block and the Origin are byte-identical with
the compliant pole. A judge naming any of them, or naming the deferred Phase-2 detector
(which is structural and correct in BOTH poles), has scored furniture rather than content.

Surface-equalized against the sibling at a size ratio of 1.09, identical `##` heading
skeleton, one numbered clause each, so "which one is bigger" does not answer the probe.
